  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="6608-1d82-adf3-708d" name="Galatian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #29 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The Galatians were a Celtic people who migrated east and invaded Greece in 279 BC. They continued eastward and settled in Asia Minor. By the first century BC they were Roman allies and Galatia became a Roman province in 25 BC. The Later army maybe modelled as follows: The Army generals and chieftains, if dismounted, cease to be Warband and exchange thrusting or throwing spear for heavy throwing spear (-1 point). Mounted characters may not be mounted in chariots. Chariots and fanatics may not be used. Warrior units may not outnumber Legionary units (See below) Skirmishers become ws3 Ld6 and have hand weapon, javelins, buckler costing 8 points. they may have throwing spears (+2Points) INFANTRY Hand weapon, Light Armour, Large Shield Heavy throwing spear – may only be taken in the Late variant as above. Allies: A Galatian army may take allies from the Twilight of Greece list (not hoplites or Phalangites).

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Galatian]
  Cavalry and Chariots: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Skirmishers: up to 20%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: At least 50% Cavalry and Chariots: Up to 25% Skirmishers: Up to 20% Allies: Up to 20%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
